From: VeraOS build qualification <veraos@local.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: allow compatible CRTC when encoder is unassigned at boot

Virtual DRM devices may have a connected connector and valid modes while the
encoder has no current CRTC assignment (crtc_id == 0).  Keep the possible_crtcs
mask check and allow its first compatible CRTC for initial mode setting.
Do not treat a different active CRTC binding as compatible.

--- a/platform/drm/cog-platform-drm.c
+++ b/platform/drm/cog-platform-drm.c
@@ -357,7 +357,10 @@ find_crtc_for_encoder(const drmModeRes *resources, const drmModeEncoder *encoder)
     for (int i = 0; i < resources->count_crtcs; i++) {
         const uint32_t crtc_mask = 1 << i;
         const uint32_t crtc_id = resources->crtcs[i];
-        if (encoder->possible_crtcs & crtc_mask && encoder->crtc_id == crtc_id) {
+        /* A cold-boot encoder may not yet have a CRTC assigned. */
+        if ((encoder->possible_crtcs & crtc_mask)
+                && (encoder->crtc_id == crtc_id
+                    || encoder->crtc_id == 0)) {
             return crtc_id;
         }
     }
